essarily mean that the ability to compose is a sufficient condition for wanting to compose. There could be other factors that influence whether someone wants to compose, such as personal interest, motivation, or external circumstances.\n\nTherefore, based on the given information, we cannot definitively conclude that if George will not compose, he can not compose. There might be other reasons why George does not want to compose, even if he has the ability to compose.\n\nThus, the correct answer is:\n**C) Uncertain**\n</think>\n<answer>\nC) Uncertain\n</answer>",
